    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n32691" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκπλοος</span></b> , 
			contr.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπλήρ-πλους</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>sailing out, leaving port,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρυφαῖον ἔ. καθίστατο</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					385
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποιεῖσθαι ἔ.,</span>=<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπλεῖν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.65
			</span></i>, etc. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βιάζεσθαι τὸν ἔ.</span>
			to force one's <i>way out,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				7.70
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴσπλους καὶ ἔ.</span> the
			right of using a port, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(7).8.12
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Amorgos</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>GDI</u>
				5687.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Chios</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>entrance of a harbour,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				367
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				1.6.18
			</span></i>.</div>
